# Line endings. This repository is edited on Windows (core.autocrlf=true),
# and its files run in Linux containers: the Docker images are built from the
# working tree (Dockerfile.worker copies src/ and skills-content/). So every
# text file is LF in the repository and in every checkout, on every OS; these
# rules take precedence over core.autocrlf. The firm's plugin copies of
# skills-content/ are LF too, so a byte-for-byte re-sync stays byte-for-byte.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Named explicitly so they stay LF whatever happens to the rule above: Linux
# reads these directly (Python, sh, the migration runner, Docker, flyctl).
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Binary: never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.doc binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
